  "description": "VEBZIN crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C130 H92 Eu4 O22 S10. From the CIF bond table, Eu1 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu2 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu1A (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu2A (Eu) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.754-3.904 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 97.42-109.45°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C130H92Eu4O22S10. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
